# Christian Petzold, Menuet in G (BWV Anh. 114, long credited to J. S. Bach), from the
# Notebook for Anna Magdalena Bach (1725), as first printed in the Bach-Gesellschaft
# Ausgabe, vol. 43.2 (1894), p. 26, No. IV. The edition prints the right hand in soprano
# clef; the notes are written here at pitch.
# Played once through: the edition repeats each half. Ornaments (the trills in bars 3, 5,
# 11, 13 and 30, and the grace note before bar 8) are left out; the notes they sit on
# are kept.
# Left hand (Advanced): the lower line as printed. Where the edition adds a second voice
# above it (bar 1's chord, bars 25, 26 and 29), only the lowest notes are taken. The
# right hand's closing chord in bar 32 is played as its top note.
# The chords are our reading of the two lines; the edition has none.
title: Minuet in G
piece: minuet-in-g
added: 2026-10-17
source: public-domain
composer: Christian Petzold
composer-died: 1733
first-published: 1894
edition: Bach-Gesellschaft Ausgabe, vol. 43.2, Breitkopf & Härtel, Leipzig, 1894, p. 26 (IMSLP #532968)
editor: Paul Graf von Waldersee
editor-died: 1906
key: G major
meter: 3/4
# The edition has no tempo mark; the tempo is ours.
tempo: 112
summary: The Notebook minuet long credited to Bach, from the 1894 Bach-Gesellschaft edition.
figure: held
# Every bar with eighth notes stays as written in Easy: the runs are the tune.
easy-keep: 1, 3, 5, 6, 7, 9, 11, 13, 14, 15

